      "body": "## Problem\n\n`grade_answer_verl` (`slime/rollout/rm_hub/math_utils.py:485`) starts with:\n\n```python\nif not ground_truth:\n    return False\nground_truth = str(ground_truth)\n```\n\nLabels are passed through from the dataset as-is (`slime/utils/data.py:272`), so a zero answer arrives as `0` or `0.0`. Both are falsy, so the guard treats them as a missing label, and every correct `\\boxed{0}` response scores 0 under `rm_type=math`. Under GRPO, a group where every sample gets 0 gives no learning signal for that prompt.\n\n#336 added `str(ground_truth)` so this function would accept non-string labels, but the falsy guard runs before that conversion.\n\nReproduction:\n\n```python\nfrom slime.rollout.rm_hub.math_utils import grade_answer_verl\ngrade_answer_verl(r\"\\boxed{0}\", 0)    # False (expected True)\ngrade_answer_verl(r\"\\boxed{0}\", 0.0)  # False (expected True)\ngrade_answer_verl(r\"\\boxed{0}\", \"0\")  # True\n```\n\n`deepscaler` (`label == \"\"`) and `gpqa` already handle numeric zero correctly. Only `math` is affected.\n\n## Fix\n\nOnly reject a missing label:\n\n```python\nif ground_truth is None or ground_truth == \"\":\n    return False\n```\n\nBehavior is unchanged for every other input, including `\"\"`, `None` and whitespace-only labels.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_rm_math.py`:\n- `test_grade_answer_verl_accepts_numeric_zero_ground_truth[0, 0.0]`: fails before this change, passes after.\n- `test_grade_answer_verl_rejects_wrong_answer_for_zero_ground_truth`: `\\boxed{1}` vs `0` is still rejected.\n- `test_grade_answer_verl_returns_false_on_missing_ground_truth[\"\", None]`: the existing empty-label test, extended to `None`.\n\n`python tests/test_rm_math.py`: 36 passed. `pre-commit run`: passed.\n\nNote: #2150 edits a line two below this one in `grade_answer_verl` (`\\fbox` support). The two changes don't conflict logically. I'll rebase if that one lands first.\n",
